DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't chase one great week.</b> The S&P jumped 5.6% this week, its best since April 2025, but fear is still extreme and November is still a losing month. Keep your regular monthly investing (DCA) instead of piling in after the rally.",
"<b>Expect another Fed hike on 9 Dec.</b> It is ~99% priced; the 4 Dec jobs report decides whether a second hike in January follows. Plan around higher rates for longer.",
"<b>Fear is easing, but stay patient.</b> CNN Fear & Greed rose to 25 from 16, and NYSE new highs (41) finally matched new lows (42). More highs than lows for several days would be a better sign of healing.",
"<b>Check your AI and chip exposure.</b> Chip stocks bounced hard, but the Nvidia–China chip probe, the Southeast Asia server halt and Huang's Congress hearings next week can swing them again. Trim back to your target mix if one theme got too big.",
"<b>Cash and short bonds still pay.</b> The 2-year Treasury yields ~4.7% and the Fed is still hiking; that money earns while you wait.",
"<b>Plan for higher loan rates.</b> The 10-year yield is back near 4.93%; fix rates where you can and avoid new variable-rate debt.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a rescue.</b> It bounced to ~$3,654 but is still ~12% below a year ago as rate hikes weigh. Keep it a small slice (e.g. 5-10%).",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> Bitcoin (~$59,850) didn't join the stock rally and sits near its 52-week low; only invest what you can afford to lose.",
"<b>Thai investors: buy slowly, stay picky.</b> The SET bounced 1.8% to 1,440 and exports are booming, but foreigners are still not buying. Favor solid dividend payers near their buy zones, and keep some cash."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 25 (24.9) = Extreme Fear, just below the 'Fear' band, up from 16 at Wednesday's close after Friday's rally; 19 a week ago and 33 a month ago. Four signals read extreme fear, two read fear, and the VIX reads neutral."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~55.0 = Elevated (up from 54.8): the US disabled another ship running the Iran blockade and a drone attack blamed on Iran killed two Italians in Kuwait."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 8.2 = extreme fear, up from 2.8 after the week's rally."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 28.8 = fear, from 25.6; NYSE had 41 new highs vs 42 new lows on Friday (WSJ)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 29.6 = fear, from 21.4."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 19.0 = extreme fear, from 7.0: demand for downside protection is easing."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. 50 on CNN's 0-100 scale = neutral; the VIX closed ~23.8 Friday, from ~26.6."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 19.4 = extreme fear, from 5.2, as money moved from Treasuries back into stocks."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 19.2 = extreme fear, from 13.2."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 78 (from 77): the US disabled another blockade runner, a drone attack blamed on Iran killed two Italians in Kuwait, and Iran claims another tanker mine hit."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 50 (unchanged): Russia fired 155 drones at Ukraine's grid; Kyiv offered a Black Sea ceasefire."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 95 (unchanged): Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey invoked their defense pact against Houthi attacks."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 11 (unchanged): Black Sea ceasefire offer pending; Iran mediation deadlocked but alive."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 31 (unchanged): no new arms-control talks or nuclear threats."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,297 at Friday's close (+1.6%); +5.6% this week, its best since April 2025."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. About 50,775 at Friday's close (+592 points); best week since October 2022."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. About 24,130 at Friday's close (+2.3%); +6.7% this week."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.93% (+8bp Friday), nearly flat on the week."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$83.1 (−0.7%, January contract); down 0.4% on the week."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. January contract ~$95.4 (−1.2%) but +3.1% on the week; the February contract trades ~$90.8."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$5.70/gal (AAA, 28 Nov), down from ~$5.90 a week ago and ~$6.35 a month ago."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,654 spot (+2.4% Friday), first weekly gain in three weeks after a 15-month low (~$3,426) on Wednesday."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$59,850 early Saturday = neutral: −1.1% in 24h; it missed Friday's stock rally."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00% after September's hike; a December hike to 4.00-4.25% is ~99% priced for 9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. October rose 0.4% MoM (est. 0.3%) and core 0.3% (est. 0.2%), a third straight upside surprise; no official YoY because of last year's data gap, well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. October rose 0.3% MoM (est. 0.4%) and 6.5% YoY, the highest since November 2022; core +0.3%."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). ~99% for a quarter point on 9 Dec; ~60% for a second hike by January (Wednesday's close)."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. ~104.0, near a 22-month high; up ~5.7% this year."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~159.6; the yen is near the 160 level where Japan has warned about intervention."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) in October; its bonds now yield ~15% (CNBC, 17 Nov)."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct; Governor Witai says the BoT aims to keep rates steady to support growth but is data-dependent; 2026 GDP forecast kept at 2.4%; next decision 23 Dec."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,440.29 on Fri 27 Nov (+25.85, +1.83%), range 1,412.08-1,440.29 (closed at the day's high); value ฿52.4B."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. −฿38.7M of Thai stocks on Fri 27 Nov (almost flat); about −฿14.5B so far in November (our tally of daily SET data)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};

